course: dictionary
lesson: 1874
title: Collaborative: working together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Collaborative means done by people working together, not alone. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues. «A cobot, or collaborative robot, is a smaller robot made to work beside people.» The clue is work beside people: a collaborative robot works with people, not on its own.
explain: Try the swap check. Put working together in place of collaborative: «a smaller robot made to work beside people» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The word can also describe a person. A collaborative team is a team that likes to share work and works well with others. Phrases like «collaborative project» and «collaborative effort» show a group doing one job together.
fact: Collaborative means done by people working together, not alone.
fact: Collaborative can describe a thing, like «a collaborative project», or a person, like «a collaborative team».
fact: «Collaborative learning» means pupils learning by working together in groups.
fact: A cobot, or collaborative robot, is a smaller robot made to work beside people; it stops if it bumps someone.
fact: Collaborative is an adjective: collaborative, more collaborative, most collaborative.
exercise: «A cobot, or collaborative robot, is a smaller robot made to work beside people.» What does collaborative mean here? | Painted bright red | Very large and heavy | *Working together with people | Working alone in a locked room
exercise: Ravi and Mia wrote one story between them, sharing every idea. Which word describes their work? | Lonely | Hurried | Silent | *Collaborative
exercise: «The class made a collaborative poster, with everyone adding one picture.» Find and copy one word that means working together. | everyone | *collaborative | poster | picture
test: «The science club gave their collaborative effort a prize.» What does collaborative mean here? | *Done by a group working together | Done with paint only | Done in secret by one person | Done very quickly
test: Which of these is a collaborative project? | A dog chases a ball in the park | *Six pupils build a model bridge together | A child sleeps all afternoon | One pupil reads a book in the library
exam: Which sentence uses collaborative correctly? | *We wrote the play as a team, a truly collaborative effort. | The clock on the wall is very collaborative. | I finished my drawing alone, so it was collaborative. | My pencil case is collaborative because it is blue.
